  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`assets/skills/habeas-bootstrap-requirements/SKILL.md` is a bundled skill with `name`/`description` front matter, so it is a site of `requirements.cli.skill_conventions`. The requirement's one MUST is that the description states when to use the skill in terms of the user's task. The description opens with \"Use when adopting Habeas in an existing codebase, when the user asks for a requirements coverage audit.\" Both triggers are user tasks, not internal mechanisms. The rest of the description says what the skill does. It ends with \"For missing test references or stale evidence, use habeas-evidence.\" The requirement allows this: it MAY name another bundled skill where an agent could confuse the two. That skill is easy to confuse with this one, so naming it is reasonable. No violation matches were listed. I found no gap.",
